1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,150
Calls Summary gives a supervisor a compact
view of the

2
00:00:03,150 --> 00:00:05,000
department's active-call workload.

3
00:00:05,449 --> 00:00:08,899
In the open Add Widget panel, choose Calls
Summary.

4
00:00:09,340 --> 00:00:13,270
This example uses four fictional calls and
the department's Routine,

5
00:00:13,460 --> 00:00:15,510
Urgent and Emergency priorities.

6
00:00:15,939 --> 00:00:19,920
A shared display can help the coordination
team notice workload, then

7
00:00:19,920 --> 00:00:23,530
turn to the detailed calls list for the
incident names and assignments.

8
00:00:23,979 --> 00:00:26,969
Use a training department when practicing
changes to the board.

9
00:00:27,120 --> 00:00:30,590
Use the gear icon at the upper right to
open configuration,

10
00:00:30,879 --> 00:00:33,069
then select Calls Summary Widget.

11
00:00:33,489 --> 00:00:36,930
Keep Show Recent Call and Show Priority
Counts on.

12
00:00:37,340 --> 00:00:39,670
Set Max Priorities to Show to All.

13
00:00:40,050 --> 00:00:44,210
This first view uses Font Size at fourteen
points, width four

14
00:00:44,300 --> 00:00:45,999
and height three grid units.

15
00:00:46,339 --> 00:00:48,609
Select Save and scroll to the summary.

16
00:00:48,970 --> 00:00:52,220
Giving the panel enough room keeps the
recent-call card and

17
00:00:52,220 --> 00:00:54,160
priority rows readable together.

18
00:00:54,390 --> 00:01:00,240
The summary shows Active four, Routine
three, Urgent one and Emergency zero.

19
00:01:00,649 --> 00:01:03,929
Its recent-call card displays the
fictional scheduled community

20
00:01:03,929 --> 00:01:07,540
standby that was already dispatched during
an earlier exercise.

21
00:01:07,889 --> 00:01:10,629
The date in its name is a historical
training label.

22
00:01:11,160 --> 00:01:14,410
Scroll to the detailed Calls table and
compare the Priority

23
00:01:14,410 --> 00:01:18,580
column: three rows are Routine, and the
warehouse alarm is Urgent.

24
00:01:18,979 --> 00:01:23,369
A priority count summarizes calls; it does
not identify which people

25
00:01:23,369 --> 00:01:25,399
or units are available to respond.

26
00:01:25,650 --> 00:01:30,460
Return to Calls Summary Widget and change
Max Priorities to Show to one.

27
00:01:30,969 --> 00:01:33,179
Select Save and inspect the board again.

28
00:01:33,669 --> 00:01:37,749
Only the Routine row, with three calls,
remains in the priority section.

29
00:01:38,179 --> 00:01:39,749
Active still shows four.

30
00:01:40,160 --> 00:01:44,970
This option limits how many priority rows
the panel displays; it does not close,

31
00:01:45,050 --> 00:01:47,630
remove or filter the underlying calls.

32
00:01:47,979 --> 00:01:52,149
A restricted display can therefore omit an
urgent category even while its

33
00:01:52,149 --> 00:01:54,140
call still contributes to the total.

34
00:01:54,240 --> 00:01:58,039
For a count-focused display, return Max
Priorities to Show to

35
00:01:58,069 --> 00:02:02,719
All, turn Show Recent Call off and keep
Show Priority Counts on.

36
00:02:03,189 --> 00:02:07,029
Increase Font Size to sixteen points, then
select Save.

37
00:02:07,450 --> 00:02:11,629
The board now shows Active four and all
three priority rows without the

38
00:02:11,629 --> 00:02:13,420
recent-call name and address card.

39
00:02:13,780 --> 00:02:15,770
This changes the summary presentation.

40
00:02:16,100 --> 00:02:18,889
The detailed calls remain available
elsewhere on the board.

41
00:02:19,340 --> 00:02:22,959
Choose a text size that people can read
from the actual viewing distance.

42
00:02:23,069 --> 00:02:26,579
Turn Show Priority Counts off as well and
select Save.

43
00:02:27,030 --> 00:02:31,729
With both optional sections hidden, the
Calls panel contains just Active four.

44
00:02:32,130 --> 00:02:35,790
The compact total may suit a secondary
display, but viewers

45
00:02:35,790 --> 00:02:39,410
can no longer see the workload's priority
distribution in that panel.

46
00:02:39,749 --> 00:02:43,449
Hiding information does not make its
underlying incidents disappear.

47
00:02:43,779 --> 00:02:48,050
Decide what your coordination team needs
to see before adopting this minimal view.

48
00:02:48,349 --> 00:02:53,100
Restore Show Recent Call and Show Priority
Counts, leave Max Priorities

49
00:02:53,100 --> 00:02:55,390
to Show at All, and select Save.

50
00:02:55,930 --> 00:02:58,689
Reload the board and inspect the complete
summary again.

51
00:02:59,200 --> 00:03:04,350
Active remains four, with Routine three,
Urgent one and Emergency zero.

52
00:03:04,889 --> 00:03:09,969
Reopen Calls Summary Widget to read back
both enabled switches, All, Font Size

53
00:03:09,969 --> 00:03:12,610
sixteen and the four-by-three dimensions.

54
00:03:13,100 --> 00:03:17,610
Checking the saved controls as well as the
visible result confirms the configuration

55
00:03:17,610 --> 00:03:19,379
the display is actually using.

56
00:03:19,629 --> 00:03:23,699
These display choices also fit departments
beyond fire and E M S.

57
00:03:24,119 --> 00:03:27,669
Security teams can summarize service calls
and patrol incidents.

58
00:03:28,070 --> 00:03:31,270
Search-and-rescue coordinators can monitor
their mission workload.

59
00:03:31,669 --> 00:03:35,270
Community paramedicine and mental health
response teams, wildland

60
00:03:35,270 --> 00:03:39,280
contractors and industrial emergency
response teams can use their own

61
00:03:39,280 --> 00:03:41,030
call priorities in the same way.

62
00:03:41,460 --> 00:03:45,089
Keep the full category view when every
priority matters, and

63
00:03:45,089 --> 00:03:48,600
consult the detailed Calls table when a
count needs investigation.

